{% comment %}
  A two-way offer: one named subscription, or buy it once.

  The purchase-plans block renders a card per selling plan the product carries.
  That is right for a product whose plans are the choice — 1, 2 and 3 month
  deliveries lined up to be compared. It is wrong for a product merchandised as
  "subscribe or don't", where those same three plans exist on the product but
  only one of them is being sold on the page: the shopper is handed a menu when
  the pitch is a single decision.

  So this block takes the plan id instead of discovering it. Everything else is
  read off the product: the price, the compare-at and the saving all come from
  the selected variant's own allocation for that plan, so a template shared
  across products stays right on each of them. The only thing typed is which
  plan, which is the one fact that cannot be inferred.

  A plan id that matches nothing on the current variant renders no subscribe
  card at all — the shopper sees the one-time card and can still buy. The editor
  gets a note saying why, since a silently missing card on a page that looks
  otherwise complete is the hardest kind of mistake to find.

  Replaces both purchase_plans and onetime. It emits the same data-cwc-offer
  attributes the plan cards do and the same data-cwc-onetime attributes the
  one-time card does, so the sticky bar, the price refresh and the add-to-cart
  all treat it as the cards they already know. That is also why it cannot sit
  beside them: the script binds one one-time control per section, and a second
  would be left dead.

  Accepts:
  - block {Object} - the simple_offer block.
  - product {Object} - product being sold.
  - current_variant {Object} - variant whose allocation is priced.
  - section_id {String} - scopes the radio group name to this section.

  Usage:
  {% render 'CWC_pdp-simple-offer__block',
    block: block,
    product: product,
    current_variant: current_variant,
    section_id: section.id
  %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  comment
    The id as typed. A merchant copying from the Shopify admin can land on a
    bare number or on a gid:// URL, and the trailing segment is the number in
    both, so the last path part is taken rather than asking for a particular
    format. `plus: 0` makes it an integer — anything non-numeric becomes 0,
    which matches no allocation and falls through to the note below.
  endcomment
  assign wanted_plan = block.settings.selling_plan_id | strip | split: '/' | last | strip | plus: 0

  comment
    Nothing found is the normal case for a template shared across products, so
    every value the card needs is seeded first and the loop only overwrites them
    on a hit. That keeps the markup below reading one flag rather than guarding
    each figure.
  endcomment
  assign has_plan = false
  assign plan_id = 0
  assign plan_price = 0
  assign plan_compare = 0
  assign plan_percent = 0

  for allocation in current_variant.selling_plan_allocations
    if allocation.selling_plan.id == wanted_plan
      assign has_plan = true
      assign plan_id = allocation.selling_plan.id
      assign plan_price = allocation.price
      assign plan_compare = allocation.compare_at_price | default: 0

      comment
        The plan states its own discount, so take it rather than deriving it.
        A plan with several adjustments discounts the first delivery by the
        first one, which is the price the card shows.
      endcomment
      for adjustment in allocation.selling_plan.price_adjustments
        if adjustment.value_type == 'percentage' and adjustment.value > 0
          assign plan_percent = adjustment.value
          break
        endif
      endfor
    endif
  endfor

  assign has_saving = false

  if has_plan

    comment
      The compare-at on the allocation is what the plan discounts against. When
      the plan carries none, the variant's own compare-at is the next best
      anchor — a product on sale still has a price to strike through.
    endcomment
    if plan_compare <= plan_price
      assign plan_compare = current_variant.price
    endif

    if plan_compare > plan_price
      assign has_saving = true
      assign saving_amount = plan_compare | minus: plan_price

      comment
        Deriving the percentage from the prices loses a fraction of a point:
        the allocation price is already rounded to the cent, so a 30% plan
        divides out to 29.99. divided_by on two integers then truncates rather
        than rounds, turning that into 29. The plan's own figure avoids both;
        the fallback multiplies by 100.0 to force float division so round has
        something left to round.
      endcomment
      if plan_percent > 0
        assign saving_percent = plan_percent | round
      else
        assign saving_percent = saving_amount | times: 100.0 | divided_by: plan_compare | round
      endif
    endif
  endif

  assign savings_style = block.settings.savings_style | default: 'percent'
  assign save_label = ''
  if has_saving and savings_style != 'none'
    comment
      Formatted before it is joined to anything: filters chain left to right, so
      'Save ' | append: amount | money hands money a string it cannot format and
      the whole label comes back blank.
    endcomment
    assign saving_money = saving_amount | money

    case savings_style
      when 'percent'
        assign save_label = 'Save ' | append: saving_percent | append: '%'
      when 'amount'
        assign save_label = 'Save ' | append: saving_money
      when 'both'
        assign save_label = 'Save ' | append: saving_percent | append: '% · ' | append: saving_money
    endcase
  endif

  assign default_choice = block.settings.default_choice | default: 'subscribe'
  assign show_onetime = block.settings.show_onetime

  comment
    Only one of the two can start selected, and the subscribe card can only take
    it if it rendered at all.
  endcomment
  assign subscribe_selected = false
  assign onetime_selected = false
  if default_choice == 'subscribe' and has_plan
    assign subscribe_selected = true
  elsif default_choice == 'onetime' and show_onetime
    assign onetime_selected = true
  endif

  assign promo_style = block.settings.promo_style | default: 'soft'

  comment
    Whether each list stands permanently or opens with its card.

    The two default differently on purpose. The subscription perks are the
    pitch — the reason to take the plan at all — and a shopper weighing the two
    options wants them in front of them whether or not they have committed yet,
    so that list stands. The one-time notes are what that choice gives up, which
    is worth saying to a shopper who has just chosen it and is nagging shown to
    one who has not, so that list opens with its card.

    Static strips are marked in the markup rather than inferred, because the
    script has to know too: it marks a closed strip inert, and doing that to one
    that is plainly visible would hide it from a screen reader alone.
  endcomment
  assign perks_static = true
  if block.settings.perks_visibility == 'selected'
    assign perks_static = false
  endif

  assign notes_static = false
  if block.settings.notes_visibility == 'always'
    assign notes_static = true
  endif
-%}

<div class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__simple-offer" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
  {%- if request.design_mode and has_plan == false -%}
    <div class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__editor-note">
      <strong>No subscription card is showing.</strong>
      {%- if block.settings.selling_plan_id == blank -%}
        Set Selling Plan ID to the plan you want sold here.
      {%- else -%}
        “{{ block.settings.selling_plan_id }}” does not match a selling plan the
        selected variant can be bought on.
        {%- if current_variant.selling_plan_allocations.size > 0 -%}
          Plans available on this variant:
          <ul>
            {%- for allocation in current_variant.selling_plan_allocations -%}
              <li>{{ allocation.selling_plan.id }} — {{ allocation.selling_plan.name }}</li>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>
        {%- else -%}
          This variant carries no selling plans at all.
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if block.settings.group_label != blank -%}
    <div class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__label">{{ block.settings.group_label }}</div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    "Nothing pre-selected" has to be announced rather than just left undone: the
    script selects the first card when it finds none selected, which would
    quietly undo the setting.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div
    class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offers"
    data-cwc-offers
    {% if default_choice == 'none' %}
      data-cwc-no-autoselect
    {% endif %}
  >
    {%- if has_plan -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        The promo strip is the card's own header rather than a banner above it,
        so the claim belongs to the offer it qualifies. It joins the card by
        pulling the two borders together — see the stylesheet.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if block.settings.promo_text != blank -%}
        <div class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__simple-offer-promo cwc_product-hero-buy-box__simple-offer-promo--{{ promo_style }}">
          {{ block.settings.promo_text }}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        data-cwc-offer puts the card in the script's offer list — that list is
        what clears every other card's selected state, so a card missing the
        attribute stays lit while another is chosen.

        data-cwc-offer-auto marks it as generated from the product's own
        allocations, which lets the script hide it when the shopper switches to a
        variant this plan cannot be bought on. Safe here for the same reason it
        is safe on the auto cards: the price came off the allocation, so there is
        no typed price left standing to fall back to.

        Both live on the tag itself and nothing may come between them: a
        whitespace-stripping tag there fuses the two into one dead attribute.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <label
        class="
          cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer
          cwc_product-hero-buy-box__simple-offer-card
          {% if block.settings.promo_text != blank %}cwc_product-hero-buy-box__simple-offer-card--joined{% endif %}
          {% if subscribe_selected %}cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer--selected{% endif %}
        "
        data-cwc-offer
        data-cwc-offer-auto
        data-cwc-offer-plan="{{ plan_id }}"
        data-cwc-offer-quantity="1"
        data-cwc-offer-variant="{{ current_variant.id }}"
        data-cwc-offer-name="{{ block.settings.subscribe_label | default: 'Subscribe & Save' | escape }}"
        data-cwc-offer-sub="{{ save_label | escape }}"
      >
        <input
          type="radio"
          name="cwc_supply_{{ section_id }}"
          class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-input"
          value="{{ block.id }}-{{ plan_id }}"
          {% if subscribe_selected %}
            checked
          {% endif %}
        >

        <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-radio" aria-hidden="true"></span>

        <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-body">
          <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__simple-offer-row">
            <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-name">
              {{ block.settings.subscribe_label | default: 'Subscribe & Save' }}
              {% if save_label != blank %}
                <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-save{% unless subscribe_selected %} cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-save--dim{% endunless %}">
                  {{ save_label }}
                </span>
              {% endif %}
            </span>

            <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-price">
              {% if has_saving %}
                <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-was" data-cwc-offer-was>{{ plan_compare | money }}</span>
              {% endif %}
              <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-now" data-cwc-offer-now>{{ plan_price | money }}</span>
            </span>
          </span>

          {% if block.settings.subscribe_sublabel != blank %}
            <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-description">{{ block.settings.subscribe_sublabel }}</span>
          {% endif %}

          {%- comment -%}
            The case for subscribing, which by default stands whether or not
            the card is the live choice — see perks_static above.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if block.settings.perks != blank -%}
            <span
              class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-details{% if perks_static %} cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-details--static{% endif %}"
              data-cwc-offer-details="{% if perks_static %}static{% endif %}"
            >
              <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-details-inner">
                <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-perks cwc-rte">{{ block.settings.perks }}</span>
              </span>
            </span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </span>
      </label>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if show_onetime and block.settings.onetime_label != blank -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        A button, not a label with a radio in it. The radio belongs to the group
        above, and a real one here would let the browser's own group behaviour
        fight the script over which option is live. The dot is drawn from the
        same class the real cards use, so the two are indistinguishable.

        It carries no data-cwc-offer-* attributes on purpose: the script finds
        the live selection by its class and then reads plan and quantity off it,
        and every one of those coming back empty is exactly right for a one-time
        purchase.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <button
        type="button"
        class="
          cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer
          cwc_product-hero-buy-box__onetime-card
          cwc_product-hero-buy-box__simple-offer-card
          {% if onetime_selected %}cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer--selected{% endif %}
        "
        data-cwc-onetime
        data-cwc-onetime-card
        data-cwc-onetime-behavior="select_only"
        data-cwc-onetime-label="{{ block.settings.onetime_label | escape }}"
      >
        <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-radio" aria-hidden="true"></span>

        <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-body">
          <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__simple-offer-row">
            <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-name">{{ block.settings.onetime_label }}</span>

            {% if current_variant != blank %}
              <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-price">
                {% comment %} {% if current_variant.compare_at_price > current_variant.price %}
                  <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-was" data-cwc-onetime-compare>
                    {{- current_variant.compare_at_price | money -}}
                  </span>
                {% endif %} {% endcomment %}
                <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-now" data-cwc-onetime-price>
                  {{- current_variant.price | money -}}
                </span>
              </span>
            {% endif %}
          </span>

          {% if block.settings.onetime_sublabel != blank %}
            <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-description">{{ block.settings.onetime_sublabel }}</span>
          {% endif %}

          {%- comment -%}
            What buying once costs the shopper. Unlike the perks above this
            opens and closes with the card by default: it is a caveat, and a
            caveat aimed at a shopper who has not chosen the option is nagging.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if block.settings.onetime_notes != blank -%}
            <span
              class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-details{% if notes_static %} cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-details--static{% endif %}"
              data-cwc-offer-details="{% if notes_static %}static{% endif %}"
            >
              <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-details-inner">
                <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-perks cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-perks--cons cwc-rte">
                  {{- block.settings.onetime_notes -}}
                </span>
              </span>
            </span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </span>
      </button>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>
